title ALES82 — Lotus's asymmetric tube drive: a different ceiling per sign, the first clip that is not odd
prompt Continue the autonomous loop — the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61, stop at custody gates.
think ALES78, ALES79, ALES80, and ALES81 each named the asymmetric / tube drive as the DRIVE family's next member. Three of the four seated members (hard clip, overdrive, wavefolder) shape the MAGNITUDE and carry the SIGN — odd functions, odd harmonics only. The tube drive is the durable, crux-shaped successor and carries no custody gate.
think The crux is the plainest asymmetry there is: split ALES78's single ceiling into ceil_pos for the positive half and ceil_neg for the negative, pinning each half to its own. When ceil_pos == ceil_neg the two branches collapse into ALES78's hard clip byte-for-byte — the family recognition, the honest proof this rung GENERALIZES rather than replaces. When they differ the map is NOT odd: tube(1000) = ceil_pos while tube(−1000) = −ceil_neg, so a symmetric input drives to an asymmetric output — a DC offset and a full set of EVEN harmonics, the tube's honest voice, the sibling of ALES81's not-odd map.
think Reused ALES78 verbatim: the pre-gain (ALES6's num/den into i64), the three gain faults (BadGain), and the ceiling law — now applied per sign. BadCeiling guards BOTH ceilings into [1, sample_max]. No new fault name beyond ALES78's three. The asymmetric pin lands every output in [−ceil_neg, ceil_pos] BEFORE the write, so the saturate is a documented no-op and the sign is always held (asymmetry lives in the magnitude, never the sign).
obs GREEN on the FIRST build across all seven laws — no RED. Proved equal ceilings against the REAL ALES78 hard drive (byte-for-byte), a hand-computed asymmetric clip (ceil_pos 1500 / ceil_neg 800 / ×2: 500→1000, 1000→1500, −300→−600, −600→−800, −100→−200), the not-odd even-harmonic signature (tube(1000)=1500 ≠ −tube(−1000)=800), each half under its own ceiling with sign held under ×8, the symmetric-ceiling degenerate recovering oddness, the span discipline, and each fault by name (BadGain, BadCeiling on either side, BadRange). tame_style_check clean.
loom witness=ales_tube_witness laws=7 result=green build=first reds=0
file lotus/tube.rye ALES82 — the asymmetric tube drive, one ceiling per sign, the first clip that is not odd.
